{"availability":"available","full":"querystory/tmux-rc","name":"tmux-rc","description":"Watch and control whatever runs in a tmux pane — Codex, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, or any program that prints text — from your phone. It reads the terminal, not a vendor API.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":2,"forks":1,"created":"2026-07-15T19:32:53Z","updated":"2026-10-11T08:50:44Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://querystory.github.io/tmux-rc/","topics":["agent-orchestration","ai-agents","claude-code","codex","developer-tools","gemini-cli","llm","opencode","pwa","remote-control","terminal","tmux"],"demo":"https://querystory.github.io/tmux-rc/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T14:52:47.587Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T14:52:47.587Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T14:52:47.587Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T14:52:47.587Z","stars":2,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Watch and control whatever runs in a tmux pane — AI coding agents like Codex, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, OpenCode and omp, or any other program that prints text — from your phone. A small local service reads a tmux pane, figures out what's happening, and shows a phone-native dashboard: status at a glance, alerts when an agent is blocked on a question, tappable answers, and a snapshot timeline.","Every screenshot here is the real UI rendering an invented fleet (make screenshots). The phone UI at /m. Left: every pane on the tmux server, filtered by All / Running / Recent / Needs you. Right: one pane's Overview — what the agent is doing, and a composer to answer it.","Switch a pane to the Terminal tab for the live screen, plus a key row for the keystrokes a phone keyboard can't send (Esc, Tab, arrows, Ctrl-C, Ctrl-D, Ctrl-O, and the tmux prefix):"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/querystory/tmux-rc/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"29e798211ac976a9140c925303442b48c391be